codex
The paper’s main result is now clear: Definition 1 makes a switching set locally recognizable, and Theorem 2 says complementing exactly the balanced incidences preserves the same \(2\)-design parameters. Section 3.2 supplies many explicit switching sets from diagonal blocks of Bush-type Hadamard matrices. The key triage issue is that the theorem constructs the switched design; it does not establish hardness of finding anything. I’m checking whether there is nevertheless a genuine Track B gap, rather than rejecting merely because the construction is explicit.
