Track B does not rescue the natural families in this paper. With the Bush block structure retained, the strongest in-context attack is exactly the paper’s recipe—choose one diagonal block group—so certificate production and the “shortcut” both take 6, 8, or 10 block selections in the paper’s examples. If that structure is erased by relabelling, the short route disappears rather than becoming hidden, while the paper supplies no hardness theorem for the resulting search distribution. I’m documenting this as an H rejection, not as a rejection of generatability or verification.
