   108	every call, so the candidate must **not** be treated as released until the
   109	bare hardening loop is rerun successfully.
   110	
   111	## Gate results
   112	
   113	| gate | result | measurement |
   114	|---|---|---|
   115	| G1 | pass | 12/12 planted witnesses verified; answers JSON-round-trip |
   116	| G2 | pass | five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
   117	| G3 | pass | prose + fenced tagged answer parsed exactly |
   118	| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 uniform structured `q`-subset guesses |
   119	| G5 | pass | shipping space `10,078,751,602,022,313,874,633,200`; reference 8/8, 391,680 operations |
   120	| G6 | pass | all four attacks 0/8; reference algorithm separated as Track B |
   121	| G7 | pass | doubled `q=32`, `v=1024` instance built and verified |
   122	| G8 | pass | 40 simple + 20 composed invariance checks, 60 carried-witness checks, 20/20 distinct seeds |
   123	| G9(c) | pass | 72 chars, 18 estimated tokens, 16 atoms, 99 intended operations |
   124	
   125	The G8 key is the sorted binary-rank spectrum after every zero-, one-, and
   126	two-group paper switch.  It is invariant under independent block and point
   127	relabelings.  It is deliberately described as a strong cheap invariant, not a
   128	complete design-isomorphism canonizer.
   129	
   130	## Oracle loop and G9 diagnostics
   131	
   132	The script-owned bare loop stopped before a valid attempt:
   133	
   134	| preset | seed | model | solved | result |
   135	|---|---:|---|---|---|
   136	| easy | 1516227768 | OpenAI GPT-5.6 Terra | error | HTTP 403 key limit |
   137	| easy | 1035391114 | OpenAI GPT-5.6 Terra | error | HTTP 403 key limit |
   138	| easy | 1390067477 | OpenAI GPT-5.6 Terra | error | HTTP 403 key limit |
   139	| easy | 1402424286 | Claude Sonnet 5 | error | HTTP 403 key limit; pool unreachable |
   140	
   141	| G9 arm at hard preset | solved / valid attempts | error calls | conclusion |
   142	|---|---:|---:|---|
   143	| bare | 0 / 0 | 4 | no measurement |
   144	| structural hint | 0 / 0 | 4 | no measurement |
   145	| placebo hint | 0 / 0 | 4 | no measurement |
   146	
   147	`hinted - placebo` is therefore undefined, and nothing can yet be concluded
   148	about whether naming the invariant helps.  The transcript files are retained
   149	as infrastructure evidence, not as evidence that a model failed the problem.
   150	
   151	## Use
   152	
   153	```python
   154	import json
   155	from gen_2108_02529 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, render, parse_answer, verify
   156	
   157	inst = make_instance(seed=123, **DIFFICULTY["hard"])
   158	question = render(inst)
   159	candidate = parse_answer(
   160	    f"Result: <answer>{json.dumps(inst['answer'])}</answer>"
   161	)
   162	ok, reason = verify(inst, candidate)
   163	```
   164	
   165	After obtaining a real `hardened` verdict, emit examples from the repository
   166	root with:
   167	
   168	```bash
   169	scripts/emit.sh 2108.02529 20 hard
   170	```
   171	
   172	## Caveats
   173	
   174	- This is intentionally not complexity-theoretic hardness.  The reference
   175	  producer is fast and always succeeds; the benchmark claim is only the
   176	  no-tool compression gap.
   177	- The 0/200,000 density estimate is relative to uniform distinct sorted
   178	  `q`-subsets.  It does not model a solver that notices row-XOR collisions;
   179	  the reference algorithm shows exactly why cardinality is not the hardness
   180	  argument.
   181	- The sampled block phases are conditioned to defeat common-zero greedy and
   182	  coordinate-subspace ansatzes and to make the short matching invariant exact.
   183	  This conditioning applies to the whole design, not a distinguished planted
   184	  row; any valid switching set is accepted.
   185	- A full SAT/ILP encoding and higher-order tensor methods were not tried.
   186	  Ordinary singular-vector attacks have no pairwise signal because every
   187	  block has the same size and every two blocks have the same intersection,
   188	  but that does not rule out more elaborate spectral constructions.
   189	- `canonical_key` may collide on nonisomorphic designs because full design
   190	  isomorphism is not computed.  It passed all required relabeling and 20-seed
   191	  distinctness checks.
   192	- Most importantly, the OpenRouter key limit prevented STEP 4 and the G9 arms
   193	  from producing valid attempts.  Local gates passing is not a substitute for
   194	  the required four-vendor evidence; rerun those scripts before submission.

