The local submission validator exposed a profile mismatch worth fixing: an incidence-structure search is classified by the repository as a discrete graph/CSP core, not `linear_algebra` merely because the implementation uses bitsets and ranks. I’m relabeling the core as `graph` (the native objects remain the paper’s incidence design) and adding an exact spectral-Gram probe; in a symmetric design its diagonal and off-diagonal entries are constant, so it has provably no row-label signal and fails under deterministic tie-breaking.
